          "title": "You'll want to know: عذرخواهی کردن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عذرخواهی کردن ('ozrkhâhi kardan) — \"to apologize\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مدیر هتل از ما عذرخواهی کرد. Modir-e hotel az mâ 'ozrkhâhi kard. The hotel manager apologized to us."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "'ozr 'excuse' + khâh 'asking' + -i + kardan. Note the letter ذ, said z."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "'ozrkhâhi kardan is built from 'ozr 'an excuse', a loan usually traced to Arabic ʿuḏr, native khâh, the present stem of khâstan 'to ask, to want', and kardan 'to do'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
