            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پس گرفتن (pas gereftan) — \"to take back; to get back (money)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پول بلیت را پس گرفتیم. Pul-e bilit râ pas gereftim. We got the ticket money back."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pas 'back' + gereftan. The opposite of pas dâdan 'to give back'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pas gereftan is built from pas 'back, behind', inherited from Middle Persian pas (EtymDB), and the native verb gereftan 'to take', usually traced to Old Persian grab-."
            }
          ]
        },
